Construct a JavaScript function that takes an array of strings as its parameter and manipulates each string so that it appears in entirely uppercase letters. For this task, you are to also design the function to be applied on data received from an API server and handle errors efficiently to ensure the final output is in the expected format. As a challenge, you are also required to identify any potential issues in the given erroneous code block that prevent it from functioning as intended and hence correct it.

```
var receivedData = ['Hello World', 'Good Morning', 'Javascript'];

function faultyUpperCase(data) {
    var processedData = [];
    for (var i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {
        processedData.push(data[i].toUpperCASe());
    }
    return processedData;
}

console.log(faultyUpperCase(receivedData));
```

The code above includes a typo in the JavaScript built-in function toUpperCase and because of that this function does not execute as intended. The erroneous "toUpperCASe()" should be corrected to "toUpperCase()". 

Let's correct the error and implement efficient error handling for the provided script. We will define an async function since we are dealing with an API server and have to handle potential errors. Inside a try-catch block, we will fetch data, convert it into JSON format and apply toUpperCase() to each item.

Here is the corrected code in Javascript:

```javascript
var receivedData = ['Hello World', 'Good Morning', 'Javascript'];

async function processToUpperCase(data) {
    var processedData = [];
    try {
        for (var i = 0; i < data.length; i++) {
            if (typeof data[i] === "string") {
                processedData.push(data[i].toUpperCase());
            } else {
                throw new Error("Non-string element found");
            }
        }
    } catch (error) {
        console.error(error);
    }
    return processedData;
}

processToUpperCase(receivedData).then(console.log);
```
The function processToUpperCase receives an array of strings, checks if each element is a string (helpful in case the array contains non-string elements), converts it to uppercase and pushes it to the processedData array. If an error occurs (Error in fetching or non-string element in array), it throws an error, which we catch and log to the console.
API fetch or other necessary steps can be added in this function according to the need. The function is kept async for future potential API interaction.

def transform_words(words):
    vowels = 'aeiou'
    transformed_words = []
    for word in words:
        if word[0].lower() in vowels:
            transformed_word = word + "imagine"
        elif word[0].lower() not in vowels:
            transformed_word = "dream" + word
        if word == word[::-1]:
            transformed_word += "reflect"
        transformed_words.append(transformed_word)
    return transformed_words
